# 必考词 Unit21
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023红宝书考研英语词汇-必考词
# 描述: 必考词Unit21核心高频词汇

{{somewhat}}{/ˈsʌmwɒt/}}{adv. 有点；稍微}}{{The results were somewhat disappointing compared to expectations.}}

{{sophisticated}}{/səˈfɪstɪkeɪtɪd/}}{adj. 复杂的；精密的；老练的}}{{The system uses sophisticated algorithms to analyze data.}}

{{source}}{/sɔːrs/}}{n. 来源；源头}}{{Renewable energy sources include solar and wind power.}}

{{specific}}{/spəˈsɪfɪk/}}{adj. 具体的；特定的}}{{Please give me a specific example to illustrate your point.}}

{{speculate}}{/ˈspekjuleɪt/}}{v. 推测；投机}}{{Scientists speculate about the origins of the universe.}}

{{sphere}}{/sfɪər/}}{n. 球体；领域}}{{She works in the sphere of international relations.}}

{{spirit}}{/ˈspɪrɪt/}}{n. 精神；灵魂}}{{The team showed great spirit during the competition.}}

{{split}}{/splɪt/}}{v. 分裂；分开；n. 裂缝}}{{The company split into two separate entities.}}

{{sponsor}}{/ˈspɒnsər/}}{n. 赞助者；v. 赞助}}{{The event was sponsored by a major corporation.}}

{{spot}}{/spɒt/}}{n. 地点；斑点；v. 发现}}{{She spotted a rare bird in the garden.}}

{{stable}}{/ˈsteɪbl/}}{adj. 稳定的；n. 马厩}}{{The patient's condition is now stable after the surgery.}}

{{stake}}{/steɪk/}}{n. 利害关系；赌注}}{{The stakes are high in this negotiation.}}

{{standard}}{/ˈstændərd/}}{n. 标准；adj. 标准的}}{{The product meets international quality standards.}}

{{stare}}{/steər/}}{v. 盯着看；凝视}}{{He stared at the screen for hours without taking a break.}}

{{status}}{/ˈsteɪtəs/}}{n. 地位；状态}}{{Social status often influences people's behavior.}}

{{steady}}{/ˈstedi/}}{adj. 稳定的；持续的}}{{The economy has shown steady growth over the past year.}}

{{steep}}{/stiːp/}}{adj. 陡峭的；急剧的}}{{There was a steep rise in housing prices last year.}}

{{stimulate}}{/ˈstɪmjuleɪt/}}{v. 刺激；激发}}{{The government introduced policies to stimulate economic growth.}}

{{strategy}}{/ˈstrætədʒi/}}{n. 策略；战略}}{{The company developed a new marketing strategy.}}

{{strengthen}}{/ˈstreŋθn/}}{v. 加强；巩固}}{{Exercise strengthens muscles and improves flexibility.}}

{{stress}}{/stres/}}{n. 压力；强调；v. 强调}}{{Work-related stress is a growing concern for many employees.}}

{{stretch}}{/stretʃ/}}{v. 伸展；延伸；n. 一段时间}}{{The desert stretches for hundreds of miles.}}

{{strict}}{/strɪkt/}}{adj. 严格的；严厉的}}{{The school has strict rules about student behavior.}}

{{strike}}{/straɪk/}}{v. 打；罢工；n. 罢工}}{{The workers went on strike for better wages.}}

{{structure}}{/ˈstrʌktʃər/}}{n. 结构；建筑物}}{{The structure of the essay should be clear and logical.}}

{{struggle}}{/ˈstrʌɡl/}}{v./n. 斗争；挣扎}}{{Many families struggle to make ends meet.}}

{{submit}}{/səbˈmɪt/}}{v. 提交；屈从}}{{Please submit your application before the deadline.}}

{{subsequent}}{/ˈsʌbsɪkwənt/}}{adj. 随后的；后来的}}{{Subsequent events proved that the decision was correct.}}

{{substance}}{/ˈsʌbstəns/}}{n. 物质；实质}}{{The chemical substance is harmful to the environment.}}

{{substantial}}{/səbˈstænʃl/}}{adj. 大量的；实质的}}{{The company made a substantial investment in research.}}

{{substitute}}{/ˈsʌbstɪtjuːt/}}{n. 替代品；v. 替代}}{{There is no substitute for hard work.}}

{{subtle}}{/ˈsʌtl/}}{adj. 微妙的；精巧的}}{{There is a subtle difference between the two words.}}

{{succeed}}{/səkˈsiːd/}}{v. 成功；继任}}{{She succeeded in getting the scholarship she applied for.}}

{{sufficient}}{/səˈfɪʃnt/}}{adj. 足够的；充分的}}{{There is sufficient evidence to support the claim.}}

{{suggest}}{/səˈdʒest/}}{v. 建议；暗示}}{{The doctor suggested that he get more rest.}}

{{summarize}}{/ˈsʌməraɪz/}}{v. 总结；概括}}{{Please summarize the main points of the article.}}

{{superior}}{/suːˈpɪəriər/}}{adj. 优越的；上级的}}{{This brand is superior in quality to its competitors.}}

{{supplement}}{/ˈsʌplɪment/}}{n. 补充；v. 增补}}{{Vitamin supplements can help fill nutritional gaps.}}

{{supply}}{/səˈplaɪ/}}{v. 供应；n. 供给}}{{The company supplies products to retailers worldwide.}}

{{supreme}}{/suːˈpriːm/}}{adj. 最高的；至上的}}{{The Supreme Court made a landmark decision on the case.}}
